# Sunway ERP backend

Java 21 · Spring Boot 3.3 · JPA · Flyway (MySQL) · package `com.erp`

## Commands

```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
mvn compile -DskipTests
mvn flyway:migrate
```

## Layering

`controller` → `service` (`@Transactional`) → `repository` → `domain`  
API shapes in `dto`. Keep controllers thin.

## Modules (packages)

| Area | Packages |
|------|-----------|
| HR & company | `hr`, `hrsettings`, root `Employee*`, `Leave*`, `CurrentJob*`, `CompanyProperty*` |
| Payroll | `salary` |
| Appraisal | `appraisal` |
| Inventory | `inventory` |
| Purchase | `purchase` |
| Sales | `sales` |
| Finance | `finance` |
| Security | `security`, `AuthService` |
| Files / PDF | `file`, `pdf`, `dto.file` |
| Shared | `common`, `DocumentSequenceService`, `exception` |

Follow patterns in the **same module** you are changing (naming, DTOs, status enums, guards).

## Multi-tenant

Use `AuthContext` for current user/company/role. Scope queries with `auth.getCurrentCompanyId()` unless super-admin. Full rules, unique-constraint pattern, and a pre-ship checklist: see `multi-tenancy.mdc`.

## Errors & API

`GlobalExceptionHandler` returns JSON with `message` (and sometimes `errors`):

- `ConflictException` → 409 (business rule / duplicate)
- `NotFoundException` → 404
- `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 field map

Prefer typed exceptions over `RuntimeException` for expected failures.

## Schema changes

`src/main/resources/db/migration/VYYYYMMDD__snake_description.sql` + matching entity/DTO in the same change.

## Git

Commit only when the user asks. No Co-authored-by or agent branding.

## Agent-maintained docs

If you introduce a reusable pattern not already in rules/skills, append it per **`capture-knowledge.mdc`** (same session, before you finish).
